{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Backpropagation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Backpropagation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"backpropagation backpropagation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Backpropagation.md","fileName":"Backpropagation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Backpropagation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 16:28\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Neural Network Training]], [[Parallel Neural Network Training]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Neural Network Training","Parallel Neural Network Training","Artificial Neural Network","Forward Propagation","Neural Network Parameter Update","Neural Credit Assignment Problem","Gradient Descent","aiassistants.epub","algorithms.epub","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Backpropagation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Backpropagation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"backpropagation backpropagation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Backpropagation.md","fileName":"Backpropagation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Backpropagation","heading":"Backpropagation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Backpropagation is the procedure used to calculate how much each neural-network parameter contributed to an output error. It propagates error information backward through the network using the chain rule.\n\nAn optimizer uses those gradients to adjust weights toward lower error over many training examples. This makes it possible to train multilayer [[Artificial Neural Network|neural networks]] as coordinated systems.\n\nTraining first uses [[Forward Propagation]] to calculate layer-by-layer activations and the final loss. Backpropagation then works from the output toward the input, calculating how weights and biases in each layer affect that loss. These derivatives support a [[Neural Network Parameter Update]] across the entire network.\n\nKelleher separates the [[Neural Credit Assignment Problem|assignment of error sensitivity]] from the optimizer's choice of weight update. During the forward pass, each neuron's weighted sum and activation are stored. The backward pass first computes a local error gradient, or delta, for output neurons; hidden deltas combine downstream deltas according to connection weights and the derivative of the hidden activation. A weight's gradient is then its destination neuron's delta multiplied by the source activation. [[Gradient Descent]] can use those gradients, but it is a separate update rule rather than the meaning of the backward calculation itself.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Neural Network Training","Parallel Neural Network Training","Artificial Neural Network","Forward Propagation","Neural Network Parameter Update","Neural Credit Assignment Problem","Gradient Descent","aiassistants.epub","algorithms.epub","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Backpropagation.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Backpropagation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"backpropagation backpropagation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Backpropagation.md","fileName":"Backpropagation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Backpropagation","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aiassistants.epub]]\n\n[[algorithms.epub]]\n\n[[bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf]]\n\n[[deeplearning_mit.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Neural Network Training","Parallel Neural Network Training","Artificial Neural Network","Forward Propagation","Neural Network Parameter Update","Neural Credit Assignment Problem","Gradient Descent","aiassistants.epub","algorithms.epub","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}